[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Breyer Variation"]
[ECO "B10"]
[Character "solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "central-pawns,e5-break"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2.d3"]
[Start "1. e4 c6"]

2. d3 d5 { Takes the centre at once. White has played a slow move, so Black can claim space. } 3. Nd2 ( 3. Nf3 Bg4 4. h3 Bxf3 5. Qxf3 e6 ) 3... e5 { Builds a big pawn centre. White's knight on d2 blocks the bishop, so White cannot easily hit the centre. } 4. Ngf3 Bd6 { Defends e5 and develops. } 5. g3 ( 5. d4 exd4 6. Bd3 Ne7 ) 5... Nf6 { Develops with an attack on e4. } 6. Bg2 O-O { King safe, and the rook goes to e8 next to back up the centre. } 7. O-O Re8 { Adds a defender to e5 and keeps the pressure on e4. Black has a big centre. If White varies, castle and keep the pawns on e5 and d5. } *
